# Local server origins

- The player's canonical local origin is exactly
  `http://127.0.0.1:8018/`.
- Serve it from the repository root with
  `python3 -m http.server 8018 --bind 127.0.0.1`.
- On PC, `minesweeper-friendly.service` is the enabled systemd user service
  that owns this process. Use `systemctl --user start/restart/status
  minesweeper-friendly.service` as appropriate instead of launching a
  second server. Source and setup are in `README.md` and `systemd/`.
- Before starting or restarting it, check whether that server is already
  running and reuse it when possible.
- Never substitute `localhost`, another hostname, or another port. IndexedDB
  scores are origin-scoped, so substitutions open a different history.
- Storage-writing automated tests use exactly `http://127.0.0.1:8099/`.
  Do not use that test origin for the player's games.
